__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
runs/
demo/
history/*.bak
!history/README.md

# Versioned predecessors: they stay on disk but do not go into the public
# repository. An adversarial review demonstrated on 2026-09-08 that three of
# four history/*.bak files were tracked -- history/README.md claimed the
# opposite -- and that plugin/herdr-plugin.toml.v2026-* carries an absolute
# home path in an EXECUTABLE line. `git rm --cached` takes them out of the
# delivery without removing them; the content stays in the history.
*.bak
plugin/*.v2026-*
plugin/bin/hoh-latest-de
policy/*.txt.v*

# Build output. Measured 2026-09-08: 18 files under build/lib/ were tracked --
# a stale copy of the source, including an older policy file. Adding the rule
# does not untrack them (see history/README.md for the same lesson); the
# exclusion from the public repository happens in D8 via the export's path
# selection.
build/
.ruff_cache/

# Stray run artifacts from ad-hoc probes executed with the repository root as
# cwd: `run_check` writes `.hoh-out-*.log` and `.hoh-scratch-*` beside its
# arena, so a probe that forgets to work in a temp directory leaves a tree
# here. Twenty such files were committed on 2026-09-11 and found by the
# export, which refuses an unclassified path -- the gate working exactly as
# intended. The files were parked outside the repository, not deleted.
c4-*/

# Repair specifications the launcher writes into a repository when a repair
# node has none of its own (`launcher._repair_spec`). They belong to the run
# that produced them, not to this repository -- one appeared at the root here
# during a self-dogfood campaign and the export refused it as unclassified.
.hoh-repair-*.md

# Caches written into the repository because something ran with HOME set to
# the repository root. The project's own gates do that deliberately -- a check
# must not read the operator's home -- and pip and pytest then put their
# caches where HOME points. The cache is not part of the delivery.
.cache/
